                  "id": "sk-instr-guide",
                  "type": "markdown",
                  "title": "AGENTS.md Context",
                  "markdown": "### AGENTS.md context for this factory stage\n\nSkills run inside the full AGENTS.md working context. The AGENTS.md for the skill's factory stage is loaded into Claude before this skill executes.\n\n| Factory Stage | AGENTS.md |\n|---|---|\n| 📋 product-requirements | [View AGENTS.md ↗](https://github.com/Darshitpandya/ai-software-factory-contract/blob/main/factories/product-requirements/AGENTS.md) |\n| 🏛 software-architecture | [View AGENTS.md ↗](https://github.com/Darshitpandya/ai-software-factory-contract/blob/main/factories/software-architecture/AGENTS.md) |\n| ⚙️ software-engineering | [View AGENTS.md ↗](https://github.com/Darshitpandya/ai-software-factory-contract/blob/main/factories/software-engineering/AGENTS.md) |\n| 🛡 security-compliance | [View AGENTS.md ↗](https://github.com/Darshitpandya/ai-software-factory-contract/blob/main/factories/security-compliance/AGENTS.md) |\n| 🚀 platform-operations | [View AGENTS.md ↗](https://github.com/Darshitpandya/ai-software-factory-contract/blob/main/factories/platform-operations/AGENTS.md) |\n\n---\n\n### Skill authority boundary\n\nA skill is **NOT:**\n- An authorization to approve its own output — only the verifier or a human can mark ACCEPTED\n- A model selector — model is defined in `FactoryRelease.runtime.defaultModel` or `stageModels`\n- A permission grant — permissions come from the MCP tool allowlist in `tools.lock.json`\n\nA skill IS:\n- A versioned, testable, SHA-256 locked procedure\n- A set of preconditions, ordered steps, required deliverables, and verification rules\n- A definition of when to escalate or stop work"
                },
                {
                  "id": "sk-instr-lock",
                  "type": "markdown",
                  "title": "SHA-256 Registry",
                  "markdown": "### SHA-256 Registry Lock\n\n```bash\n# verify all 15 skill digests match skills.lock.json\npnpm factory registry:verify\n\n# recompute after editing any SKILL.md\npnpm lock-components\n```\n\nThe first 16 hex characters of the SHA-256 are shown in the Details panel above. The full digest is in `factory-releases/skills.lock.json`.\n\n**Any SKILL.md edit without running `pnpm lock-components` fails CI and blocks all factory runs using that release.**"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
